  takes shape but with the physical  characteristics of a particular  substance and so just as with  transmutation a conjurer needs to have  an innate understanding  of the objects that they are crafting  because it's not a simple task of saying  oh i want to will a chain into existence  because you need to make certain  decisions regarding what kind of metal  that chain would be how big and thick  the links are how many links there are  going to be  are they rusty are they smooth etc etc  all sorts of stuff like that that a  conjurer needs to envisage  each and every time they create  something and according to izunavi a nen  user invoking conjuration  should only decide what to conjure after  extraordinarily careful consideration  because it takes an astonishing amount  of concentration  and training but it's not quite that  simple because conjurers here are  invoking the power of creation  and so this also gives them the ability  to alter the established properties of  constructs that they make and this is  because if they were only capable of  making things that already exist in  reality  then conjuration would be a rather  redundant utility ability so the main  crux of conjuration has more to do with  how a user alters objects that they  craft  and that grants us a huge variety of  creative results  before we get into that though i do need  to check in with professor hisoka for  his personality test and according to  him  conjurers tend to be highly strong  overly serious and sometimes  nervous individuals they are generally  highly analytical and invoke their craft  for very deliberate and logical purposes  and i have to say of all of the  personality definitions thus far hisoka  is pretty bang on with this one  although there are always going to be  exceptions yes chitu i'm looking at you  but to get into some more specifics let  us start with the most famous of  conjurers in the series being karapika  so i used him as an example before in  regards to conjuring chains but karapika  is quite a special conjurer in many ways  and he quite rapidly mastered the art  form to suit his own personal needs  which has resulted in the option of  conjuring five different chains in  battle  each of which has a specific purpose and  often a special conjured end  such as the dowsing chain which looks  like a simple ball but we get more and  more complex with examples like the holy  chain which takes the form of a detailed  little cross for healing via enhancement  and i'm not going to go through all of  them here because graphica is the kind  of men user that you could spend a whole  video on just  explaining the abilities of especially  due to his dual typing but krapika is so  advanced that he has the ability to  conjure any of these chains into  existence at a moment's notice which  means that he has undergone some pretty  intensive vision training in order to do  so but moving on to a more simplistic  application of conjuration i would  present cortopi a very underrated and  undefeated member of the phantom troop  who has a handy little ability known as  gallery fake this allows core topi to  touch a real-life object with his left  hand  and produce an exact replica of it with  his right hand but why would you want to  do this because earlier i said that  conjuring objects that already exist is  more or less pointless well there's a  bit more to gallery fake than that  although i do firstly want to recognize  that due to the nature of this ability  cortopi does not have to engage in any  strict mental work he just needs to  touch an object and then bam he can make  an exact atomically perfect copy which  is actually kind of insane but in  addition to this coretopia is then able  to track the movements of all of the  copied objects and on top of everything  after 24 hours the copied objects vanish  from existence entirely and when i say  objects  yes cortopi can use gallery fake on  people but it will only replicate their  bodies meaning that he would essentially  create a lifeless corpse which was used  on one occasion to fake the deaths of  the phantom troop during the york new  city arc  as well as incredibly effectively in  combination with other borrowed powers  by crollow  in heaven's arena so it's quite a simple  sounding yet very intriguing use of  conjuration to be able to perfectly  replicate objects with minimal effort  but for a strictly limited time period  it's a pretty wonderful balance  and perfect for a group of thieves to  make use of and staying with the phantom  troop for now another very well known  conjurer here would have to be shizuku  who takes the discipline a bit further  than we've explored thus far and uses  her aura to bring a living vacuum  cleaner by the name of blinky into  existence who can suck  up seemingly an infinity of non-living  objects but the main thing i want to  highlight here is a whole new branch of  conjuration  in regards to making living things which  actually gives rise to an entire  subsection of nan being the creation of  nine beasts  a category that i have already explored  before on the channel but it basically  refers to living then construct stuff  like blinky but a slew of other great  examples would be every other guardian  spirit beast present in the succession  war they were all products of the sea  dome which was originally conjured into  existence by the first king of the kakin  empire which then used its particular  unique abilities in combination with  blood from all the princes to craft a  series of nine beasts now there is of  course another affinity you can use to  make nun beasts which is a mission but  the large majority of living nang  creations tend to be conjuration because  it is a more natural path to achieve the  end result  and the only reason really why you would  use emission instead is if conjuration  is too far removed from one's personal  spot on the nen ring furthermore the use  of nen beast does usually require  dipping into some manipulation in order  to control them with that said the first  example being blinky  until stated otherwise appears to be a  use of pure conjuration although shizuku  does need to very specifically tell  blinky what to do  which may imply a form of manipulation  or it could just be a very naturally  obedient vacuum  and for a similar example we need to  travel all the way to the chimera  antarctic to discover a certain kite who  is a natural conjurer and his crazy  slots ability  is very much the epitome of phenomenal  maximization of this affinity much like  shizuku it begins with kite conjuring a  living existence  a clown thing to be precise which does  appear to have a life and personality of  its own and kite would not seem to be  capable of manipulating it at all but  the clown then activates a roulette and  whatever number that rule it lands on  results in kite conjuring a specific  weapon from the clown now saying it like  that crazy slot sounds like very  roundabout way of achieving kait's goal  i mean for example if he needs a scythe  then why not go ahead and conjure a  scythe himself without going through the  risk of gambling and while that's  because taking that risk is  everything it is what makes crazy slot  so powerful in the world of men adding  restrictions and limitations  is almost a straightforward multiplier  of power of the resulting ability in  question  and the more difficult the restriction  the greater that multiplication is going  to be  and this is a pretty damn heavy  restriction at any given time kite can  only fight with a random weapon  and he cannot re-roll until he actually  uses the weapon so when it does land on  the slot number representing the scythe  it results in a weapon of incredible  power but kite is then forced to use  that  even in situations that don't  necessarily call for the scythe however  it doesn't even end there because kite  has placed a further restriction on the  scythe itself and assumingly all of the  weapons and crazy slots but in this  particular example  kite can only use the scythe one way to  invoke the silent waltz technique that  is literally the only thing he can use  it for but it results in one of the most  devastatingly powerful attacks that we  have ever seen in nen user before  thanks essentially to a double  multiplying factor applied to pure  conjuration so while karapika might be  the most famous conjuring hunt hunter i  have no reservations in stating that  kind is probably the greatest conjurer  that we have encountered thus far  especially because he doesn't dip into  other affinities for crazy slots this is  just pure conjuration  taken to its extreme but now from the  greatest user to probably the  greatest failure of conjuration let's  briefly very briefly look at chitu and  look i put this guy as the undisputed  number one on my top five worst nine  users list  and for very good reason because he does  incredibly poorly thought out things  like conjure a crossbow that fires an  arrow slower than chito himself can  travel and i guess the claw at the end  of said crossbow might be mildly useful  but all around this is completely  counter-intuitive to chitu's needs as  well as the goal of conjuration in  general although to be fair chitu did  possess one incredibly impressive  ability which was the tag hatsu in which  he actually conjured a pocket dimension  which is pretty astounding use of nun  although unfortunately the rules he  applied to this dimension  also did not suit his needs and  furthermore in order to create it a very  harsh restriction was applied whereby if  tutu ever lost his game of tag then he  would never be able to use the ability  again which of course he did when he was  easily outwitted by moral but for what i  would say is a better example of pocket  dimensions we do have to mention the  figure of nov a conjurer who took  everything that was impressive about  cheetah's ability  and actually made it good which presents  itself in the hide and seekatsu so nov's  pocket dimension consisted of a four  level mansion structure with 21 rooms of  varying sizes and also rooms that were  entirely separate from one another with  nov being the only individual  capable of traveling between them in  addition to this he could also conjure  portal style entrances and exits do his  pocket dimension back to the real world  and create an extensive network that had  the potential to completely  revolutionize both travel and storage  all of which was integral during the  chimera and r but it's just insane to  think about because at the very least i  cannot imagine the sheer aura output  that nov would have needed to dish into  this ability in order to conjure it in  the first place especially because there  are no real known individual drawbacks  to nov himself there are plenty of  restrictions but  none that affect nov which means that  this pocket dimension would have come  at an exorbitantly high or a cost and  just to cover a few more conjurers  gentry was another great one to bring up  the main antagonist of greed island who  was able to conjure lethal and  non-removable bombs  onto his victims and activate them  through a series of restrictions  including genthru needing to reveal  everything about his own abilities to  said victims  and even offering a dispel condition  which was to touch ganthru and say i  caught the bomber but as much crap as i  will give gen through  as a villain in the series countdown is  still a pretty scary hatsu and it goes  on to show the terrifying potency of a  conjurer who is consumed by a less than  savory task such as mass murder for  example  and combined with little flower gentra  has a pretty damn powerful set of  abilities and also from some more recent  hunter hunter there was a conjurer who  caught my eye by the name of henry  bigendofno which is one of those classic  tagashi examples of  how annoying can i make this name to  pronounce yeah  henry bikindofno that'll do but with  that said he has a really fun  conjuration ability known as biohazard  in which he can turn any device he  touches into a living creature which is  a very different exploration of  conjuration than we've encountered  elsewhere because usually conjuration  creates an object from aura but this is  a more strange application whereby henry  is manipulating the structure of an  existing object  and giving it life through aura and  speaking of manipulation he can also  then go on  to issue orders to his living creations  so manipulation is almost certainly  involved here as well but that is a  fairly simple breakdown of conjuration  it can be used for really whatever the  user wants so long as their needs  require an object or a living thing  to fulfill which in 99 of cases you can  structure abilities to do exactly that  i would also say that conjuration is  probably one of the more underrated nand  disciplines along with manipulation and  emission because they sound really  straightforward and like there's not a  lot of opportunity for really extensive  and creative use but that  could not be further from the truth but  what do you guys think please do leave  your thoughts in the comments below or  even join my discord server and if  you're keen for some more hunt hunter  content then please do feel free to  check out some of my other videos  or even subscribe to the channel for  regular hunt hunter glory delivered  straight into your youtube feed  but for now this has been the new world  review and i'll see you next time

